I know.  However... I don't think a reasonable fee is the difference
between the selling and buying prices, especially if charisma is low.
This is also a poor method of appraising scrolls of scare monster,
cursed items which can't be dropped, etc. 

It's also counterintuitive for new players.  You shouldn't have to
sell an item when all you want to do is ask what it's worth.  This
should be implemented as part of #chat.

But most of all, I wanted identification.  In order to appraise an 
item the shopkeeper must figure out what the item is.  He/she should
be happy to sell me that information.  "Thank you for the 50gp...
yes, that's a +3 cloak of indifference. For another 100gp, I'll even
tell you what it does.  If you'd prefer, I'll buy it for 300gp.  You
won't get a better price anywhere else in the dungeon."

